            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19248,
            "text": "Created attachment 3950\nAvoid get0() of character environment name\n\nOne subtle difference of `exists()`+`get()` vs. `get0()` is the latter doesn't accept character environments:\n\n```\nx = 1\nget(\"x\", \".GlobalEnv\")\n# [1] 1\nexists(\"x\", \".GlobalEnv\")\n# [1] TRUE\nget0(\"x\", \".GlobalEnv\")\n# Error in get0(\"x\", \".GlobalEnv\") : invalid 'envir' argument\n```\n\nThat means r68579 to change `getClassDef()` to use `get0()` had a subtle back-compatibility problem, in particular with its wrapper `isClass()`:\n\n```\nsetClass(\"A\", slots=c(x=\"numeric\"))\nsetClass(\"B\", contains=\"A\")\nb_def <- getClassDef(\"B\")\nremoveClass(\"A\")                                                                                                                                                  \n\ncompleteExtends(b_def)\n# Error in get0(cname, where, inherits = inherits) : \n#   invalid 'envir' argument\n\ntraceback()\n# 5: get0(cname, where, inherits = inherits)\n# 4: getClassDef(Class, where)\n# 3: isClass(by, where = packageSlot(ext[[i]]))\n# 2: .walkClassGraph(ClassDef, \"contains\", where, attr(ext, \"conflicts\"))\n# 1: completeExtends(b_def)\n```\n\nThe problem is, `isClass()` is passing a character string _via_ `packageSlot()`, which used to work."
          }
        ]
